Yes, very good.

575
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:44,520
Girl, close your eyes for a moment.

576
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,880
Yes, very good.

577
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:48,400
I haven't taken the close-up yet.

578
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,800
This doesn't need a close-up, right?

579
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,360
Very good.

580
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,320
Look at him.

581
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:57,440
Look up.

582
00:19:57,440 --> 00:20:01,120
Yes, very good.

583
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:04,080
Go.

584
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:11,480
Yes, hold him.

585
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:13,840
Does it smell good?

586
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:19,320
Does it smell good?

587
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:26,080
Okay.

588
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:30,480
Come over here.

589
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:30,840
What's wrong?

590
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:33,760
You prefer to hold with your right hand?

591
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:34,240
Yes.

592
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,600
Men on the left,
women on the right, right?

593
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,800
Are you...

594
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,240
Isn't it, men on the left,
women on the right?

595
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:39,400
Yes.

596
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,200
Why is that?

597
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:41,800
Is there some obsession with this?

598
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:43,400
No obsession.

599
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:47,920
I'll throw you down.

600
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:49,480
Call out louder.

601
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,360
Pig's squeal.

602
00:20:51,360 --> 00:20:53,480
The sun is really nice right now.

603
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:54,360
There's still a bit of light.

604
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:58,920
Quickly take a photo for you.

605
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:00,840
This one is actually okay too.

606
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:07,680
("Bossy CEO" starts his photography side hustle)
Let me take a couple for you.

607
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:11,040
Absolutely stunning.

608
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:14,200
I should do some creation here, right?

609
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:16,800
I think it automatically
lengthens things.

610
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:17,280
Really?

611
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,280
Absolutely stunning.

612
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,560
The feeling is coming back.

613
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:22,840
Can I stand a little higher?

614
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:26,880
Be careful.

615
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:27,480
Are you standing steady?

616
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:28,800
I can.

617
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:34,960
Just focus on your pose.

618
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:38,600
Absolutely stunning.

619
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:44,760
(Seriously creating)
Actually, this spot is pretty good too.

620
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,360
(Shot by Zhou Youling)
Absolutely stunning.

621
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:50,560
Amazing, this light.

622
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:52,400
My legs look so long.

623
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,480
Yeah, I found
an absolutely stunning scene.

624
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,200
You're amazing.

625
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,480
We almost missed it.

626
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:58,160
I was heading straight this way.

627
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:58,960
Right.

628
00:21:58,960 --> 00:21:59,720
As soon as I saw this side,

629
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:01,680
the creative spark hit me.

630
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:03,240
I want to post those few today

631
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,680
without retouching.

632
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:05,920
Haven't you noticed that all photos

633
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:07,440
(A 'bossy CEO' production is always a masterpiece)
I take of you don't need retouching?

634
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,360
None of them need retouching.

635
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,280
But you said it could be better
with a little retouching.

636
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,320
But I don't think
that they need retouching.

637
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,960
Right, but a little retouching
would make it top-tier.

638
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,680
After others see it,

639
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:18,000
they'd want them as wallpaper.

640
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,040
Then why isn't it your wallpaper?

641
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:21,440
Then why isn't it your wallpaper?

642
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:28,120
(When faced with a hard question, he just stops talking)
Digging your own grave.

643
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,960
Stir-fried chicken and river shrimp.

644
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:30,960
Let's eat spicy food.

645
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:32,080
Okay, let's eat spicy food.

646
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,160
Alright.

647
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:35,040
Cheers with chopsticks.

648
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:37,920
This is pickled vegetables
with bamboo shoots and edamame.

649
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,280
(Thoughtful)
Put it on your side.

650
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:42,480
It's just edamame.

651
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:49,160
Great.

652
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:50,800
Have you...

653
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:51,680
How many meals have you eaten

654
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,560
since leaving the house,

655
00:22:53,560 --> 00:22:57,560
(Caring)
or eating alone?

656
00:22:57,560 --> 00:22:59,040
I've only eaten twice.

657
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:00,880
Once with Ji Yu.

658
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:01,600
Once in Hainan.

659
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:02,320
And what else?

660
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:04,120
And then with you.

661
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:06,080
Which time?

662
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:07,760
The Snail Maiden.

663
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:12,400
(Thinking)
No.

664
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,840
(Giving more hints)
One-on-one,

665
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:22,080
ate at a restaurant.

666
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,440
Still can't remember?

667
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:25,400
Don't interrupt me.

668
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:27,400
It didn't happen in Hainan.

669
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:30,360
(Muttering)
In Hainan, I only ate with Ji Yu once.

670
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:32,480
After we came back,

671
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:35,750
(Memory returns)
Liyao Village.

672
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:37,760
(It's in Episode 8)

673
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:43,720
Looks great.

674
00:23:43,720 --> 00:23:46,040
(Jealous mode activated)
What did you eat with Ji Yu that day?

675
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:48,680
You've asked so many times.

676
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:51,680
You've even asked Ji Yu.

677
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:54,000
(Caring)
Western food?

678
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:54,840
It wasn't exactly Western food.

679
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:57,960
It was just like a...

680
00:23:57,960 --> 00:24:00,520
(Really cares)
What time did you go eat?

681
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:02,840
We probably started eating around six

682
00:24:02,840 --> 00:24:04,480
and finished around seven.

683
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:07,120
Then we went for a walk by the sea.

684
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:07,840
After the walk,

685
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:11,080
we said

686
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:12,120
as you were having
your birthday that night,

687
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:14,400
so we headed back early to set up.

688
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:16,080
Talked about
how to celebrate my birthday?

689
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:19,120
What was your task?

690
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:20,920
To keep you occupied.

691
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,680
To keep you occupied after you got back

692
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:26,000
(Realization dawns)
and check if you had a phone on you.

693
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,120
So,

694
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:28,920
when I came back,

695
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:30,480
(Replaying the scene)
you rushed up to me immediately

696
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:35,680
to keep me occupied.

697
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:39,440
Another misunderstanding.

698
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:43,360
Eating this is making me so hot.

699
00:24:43,360 --> 00:24:45,320
That was picking ten questions to answer.

700
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:45,920
What?

701
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:46,800
I mean

702
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:47,800
that (Love Actually) travel plan.

703
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:49,920
It's about picking
ten questions to answer.

704
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:50,560
I see.

705
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:54,040
Wait a minute.

706
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:59,240
(Q: The biggest regret)
The biggest regret.

707
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:05,680
What I wrote down was

708
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:06,800
not being brave enough

709
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:09,040
to express my feelings.

710
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:11,240
(Mr. Zhou is not satisfied)
That's a cop-out.

711
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:16,640
You wish I had written about you, right?

712
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:17,800
(Starting to coax)
What was your biggest regret?

713
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:21,560
I didn't confess
to Zhou Youling in person.

714
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:22,600
And what?

715
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:23,920
Which version of myself
do I want to affirm most?

716
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:25,560
The one I want to affirm most
is the version of me who,

717
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:29,600
after returning to Shanghai,
bravely asked Zhou Youling out, right?

718
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:32,000
Is it okay
to write it like that, Mister?

719
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:40,080
At least you should write like that.

720
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:41,320
If you didn't write it that way,
then forget it.

721
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:46,280
I won't write it that way either.

722
00:25:46,280 --> 00:25:50,120
It goes well with rice.

723
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:52,760
Finished eating. Let's go.

724
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:53,360
Mr. Zhou,

725
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:53,960
for your visit to Wuzhen today,

726
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:55,000
have we been good hosts?

727
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:56,000
It's okay.

728
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,560
There's another activity.

729
00:25:57,560 --> 00:26:00,736
Please look forward to it, Mr. Zhou.

730
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:04,640
(Beijing)

731
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:07,440
We've arrived at the place to eat now.

732
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,800
We are both absolutely starving.

733
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:12,240
It smells so good here.

734
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:16,680
It looks really delicious.

735
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:18,720
Angeli's beef fried sauce noodles.

736
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:21,400
Okay, thank you.

737
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:23,280
Shall I just mix it directly?

738
00:26:23,280 --> 00:26:23,880
Is that okay?

739
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:25,560
You do it.

740
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:29,240
I'll send a photo to the group chat
to make them jealous.

741
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:35,760
I can already smell the aroma.

742
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:36,440
Thank you.

743
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:38,360
Thank you.

744
00:26:38,360 --> 00:26:39,480
Let me take this away for you.

745
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:39,640
Okay.

746
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:43,520
Okay.

747
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:45,920
Okay, thank you.

748
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:47,680
(You're being too formal)
Can we stop saying thank you?

749
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:48,520
Okay.

750
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:52,320
Thank you.

751
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:53,800
This is delicious.

752
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:56,280
That's Sautéed Pork Liver,
Pork Kidney and Pork Tenderloin.

753
00:26:56,280 --> 00:26:59,600
But people in Wuhan
generally like spicy food.

754
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:01,440
I think Wuhan stir-fries are very spicy.

755
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:03,440
Yes.

756
00:27:03,440 --> 00:27:06,640
What fun things are there
to do in Wuhan?

757
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:09,040
I'll take you to Yellow Crane Tower.

758
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:12,080
I'm not really into
visiting tourist spots.

759
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:15,600
But you took me
to visit tourist spots today.

760
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:19,880
Sorry.

761
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:23,320
What can couples actually do together?

762
00:27:23,320 --> 00:27:24,840
What do you think we can do?

763
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:27,920
Isn't it just spending time
with each other,

764
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:28,720
eating and chatting?

765
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:30,680
What? Why are you laughing like that?

766
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:32,640
Why are you smiling like that?

767
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:34,560
Isn't it just eating, chatting,
and watching movies?

768
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:37,200
What else can you do on a date?

769
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:38,360
I feel like our time in the house,

770
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:40,960
the things we did were just...

771
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:43,240
Just a set of fixed routines
for everyone,

772
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,640
eating, chatting, and watching movies.

773
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:45,840
Right.

774
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:47,520
And then, yeah.

775
00:27:47,520 --> 00:27:49,360
Maybe for me, I would add sports,

776
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:53,920
like playing ball
or working out together.

777
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:54,280
Yeah.

778
00:27:54,280 --> 00:27:55,320
But I think

779
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:57,120
isn't life made up of these things?

780
00:27:57,120 --> 00:27:58,120
Spending time together

781
00:27:58,120 --> 00:28:01,480
and doing these things together.

782
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:04,640
Otherwise, there's no interaction.

783
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:05,800
Are you full?

784
00:28:05,800 --> 00:28:08,160
Almost.

785
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:09,240
Let's go then.

786
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:10,680
Let's go.

787
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:11,120
Go.

788
00:28:11,120 --> 00:28:14,400
Okay.

789
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:16,200
Let's head out!

790
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:18,120
The last time I was in Beijing

791
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:21,200
was really three years ago.

792
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:23,360
That's crazy.

793
00:28:23,360 --> 00:28:25,000
What feeling does Beijing

794
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:27,600
give you?

795
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:32,840
Beijing feels a bit more formal to me.

796
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:34,840
My uncle is also in Beijing.

797
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:37,320
My uncle and aunt are also in Beijing.

798
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:39,600
I didn't even tell them I was coming.

799
00:28:39,600 --> 00:28:47,760
Do you want to meet them?

800
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:49,080
You're silent.

801
00:28:49,080 --> 00:28:50,160
No answer.

802
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:51,080
Let's go.

803
00:28:51,080 --> 00:28:51,840
Let's go.

804
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:54,360
Punch it,

805
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:56,480
and new destination right now.

806
00:28:56,480 --> 00:29:01,240
Let my uncle take a look first.

807
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,680
Is this a place for afternoon tea?

808
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:04,880
I don't know.

809
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:05,600
I think

810
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:07,560
I've been here.

811
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:09,320
I usually never come here.

812
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:11,080
It's too crowded.

813
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:12,960
You can barely move.

814
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:14,920
Then why did you bring me here?

815
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:16,960
To let you experience being a tourist.

816
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:17,760
The tourist vibe.

817
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:19,000
So I can barely move?

818
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:21,360
So you can barely move.

819
00:29:21,360 --> 00:29:23,040
Unable to move.

820
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:25,080
Unable to stop.

821
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,080
What does "unable to stop" mean?

822
00:29:26,080 --> 00:29:27,520
Unable to move and unable to stop

823
00:29:27,520 --> 00:29:28,800
are two different things.

824
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:31,320
Don't lump them together.

825
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:35,360
Oh no, my IQ is failing me again.

826
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:36,320
Although being unable to stop

827
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:40,520
might lead to being unable to move.

828
00:29:40,520 --> 00:29:42,960
What are you talking about?

829
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:45,000
Nothing.

830
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:47,200
You're talking nonsense with me.

831
00:29:47,200 --> 00:29:48,560
You started talking nonsense.

832
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:49,840
So I just played along
and talked nonsense.

833
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:51,280
No, I just thought of the phrase.

834
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:53,280
Can't I just say something random?

835
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:54,920
What's wrong with just saying it?

836
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:56,640
It's not like I'm doing anything.

837
00:29:56,640 --> 00:30:00,360
Unable to stop, unable to move.

838
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:01,480
Unable to stop.

839
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:02,840
Stop...

840
00:30:02,840 --> 00:30:03,360
Stop...

841
00:30:03,360 --> 00:30:04,720
"Stop" and shop.

842
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:06,360
(Sudden idiom chain)
Shop...

843
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:08,200
Shop what?

844
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:08,760
Stuck, aren't you?

845
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:09,120
Shop...

846
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:11,960
Dumbfounded huh?

847
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:13,920
Shop until you drop the ball.

848
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:14,880
Is that even a phrase?

849
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:15,640
Yes.

850
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:17,680
Shop until you drop the ball.

851
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:19,800
Ball...

852
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:22,320
Ballistic.

853
